Hi Patricia and Lauren,

Attached are the approved exchange plan and a separate workbook with the thre=
e desk checks from this morning. Robert approved the plan and record layout a=
t 13:10. The allocation remains 10 samples in each of the 24, 48 and 72 h gro=
ups; we still need to set the study date.

The three examples each led back to one preparation row: P01 for MX24-03, P02=
 for MX48-03 and P03 for MX72-03. The workbook records the planned and actual=
 desk times separately. The differences there are for the paperwork rehearsal=
, not differences in exchange interval.

For the study records, please match the sample ID and preparation date togeth=
er against Patricia's register and retain the row reference. If the preparati=
on date is missing or unreadable, send the entry back to Patricia to confirm =
it; please don't match it by group alone. Lauren, please continue to enter th=
e planned and actual times in separate fields, leaving actual time blank unti=
l it is read from the clock.

Thank you all for working through the examples.

Melissa

